# A short research article in the layout of a journal: the title, the authors and the abstract across the page and the
# body in two Columns, where the headings, the figures and the table flow from one column to the next. The sections are
# numbered headings (Numbered: 1, 2, 2.1...), and the running head of every page but the first is the section in
# effect ({heading 1: first}, the first section that starts on the page, in a Page overlay with Pages: not-first). The figures and the table have numbered captions
# ("Figure 1.", "Table 1.") that the text cites with {number of: id} and {page of: id}, the citations are the numbers
# of the items of the reference list ([{number of: ref-id}], each one a link to its item) and three footnotes sit at
# the bottom of the page of their call. The affiliation marks are superscript styled runs ([1]{sup}, Position:
# superscript). Hyphenation in US English and optimal line breaking give the justified columns an even colour.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 24mm 18mm 22mm 18mm
	Title: Occupancy of integrated nest bricks by common swifts in retrofitted housing
	Subject: Four breeding seasons of nest brick monitoring on twelve retrofitted apartment blocks in Northfield
	Author: Maren Holt, Tomás Ferreira, Aiyana Brooks
	Keywords: Apus apus, nest bricks, building retrofit, urban birds, monitoring
	Language: en-US
